%% DM26-0670

%% Asking a running agent for its configuration, and the file written from the answer, as built (2026-11-05,
%% docs/architecture/dynamic-settings.md, "Asking an agent what is in force"). Signing the file and how it reaches the agent:
%% general/configuration_authoring. How a value then reaches the actor that holds it: general/held_agent_and_dynamic_setting.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant Tool as polar-running-config
    participant Bk as Cassini broker
    participant Other as every other agent
    participant Sup as the agent's<br/>InfrastructureSupervisor
    participant Cfg as its ConfigurationActor
    participant Sign as polar-sign

    Admin->>Tool: polar-running-config jira-observer --user alice, through just port-forwards-up broker
    Tool->>Bk: connect with alice's certificate
    Tool->>Bk: subscribe polar-running-configuration-answers
    alt policy permits: the seed's rule for Group::"config-readers", which config-writers is in
        Bk-->>Tool: subscribed
    else a person's certificate names no topics, so nothing else admits one
        Bk-->>Tool: refused, and the tool says what is missing: the group, or the rules
    end
    Tool->>Bk: publish on polar-running-configuration-questions: a question signed with alice's key,<br/>under its own signing domain: its id, the agent it is for, and a window of at most 5 minutes
    Note over Bk: the same rule, for the publish, and the broker stamps who sent it
    Bk->>Other: delivered: every agent hears every question
    Other->>Other: it says it is for someone else: not read any further
    Bk->>Sup: delivered, stamped published_by
    Sup->>Cfg: the question, off the supervisor's own thread
    Cfg->>Cfg: the signature holds, under that domain and no other. It is a question, for this agent,<br/>and its signer is who the broker says sent it
    Cfg->>Cfg: Cedar: Action::"read-configuration" on Agent::"jira-observer": the seed permits config-readers.<br/>Where it is silent, the certificate: c:update-configuration
    Cfg->>Cfg: not revoked, and within its time
    alt any of those refuses
        Cfg-->>Sup: why
        Note over Sup: a warning naming the asker, and no answer: the tool's wait ends and it says to look there
    else admitted
        Cfg-->>Sup: every declared variable: its value, where it came from, whether it is Dynamic.<br/>A secret's value, or one that repeats it, is withheld. The last version applied, and each runtime section's version, never its body
        Sup->>Bk: publish on polar-running-configuration-answers, with its identity
        Bk->>Tool: delivered to whoever may listen
        Tool->>Tool: its id, that agent, and stamped with that workload: otherwise not the answer
        Tool-->>Admin: the answer as JSON
    end

    opt --template
        Tool->>Sign: polar-sign template jira-observer --settings --running -
        Sign-->>Admin: the file: version one above the last applied. What a signed document holds is a live line, and the rest<br/>are commented out with their value and where it came from, so signing does not pin what the render gave
        Admin->>Sign: edit it, polar-sign sign --push
        Note over Admin,Cfg: Applied, the document replaces every override before it: what it does not name goes back to the rendered value,<br/>and asks Cedar for that variable too. A running agent and a restarted one then agree
    end
